# ANTI-REGRESSION POSITIVE — the control for the `&`-in-an-OWNING-POSITION
# class. A named `&`-BIND (`int y = &c.fd`) already rejects, correctly:
#
#     error[E_LocalBorrowBind]: cannot bind a mutable borrow (`&`) to a name —
#     a place has one exclusive writer, and a named `&`-binding would alias a
#     second writable path to it.
#
# CORRECT TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C and LLVM both refuse to build);
# `ggdef` rejects it too.
#
# It is the same `&c.fd` operand as the seven defective costumes
# (`sound_amp_owning_position_*.gg`), landing in an owning position — and this
# is the one position where production already does the right thing. Keeping it
# live means the class fix cannot be "reject `&` of a by-value field
# everywhere" in a way that changes THIS diagnostic: a user who writes the bind
# should keep getting the specific, actionable `E_LocalBorrowBind` message with
# its two suggested fixes, not a generic owning-position error.
#
# The `fd` seed is COMPUTED, not a literal, matching its siblings.
struct Counter:
    int fd

int seed():
    return 10

void main():
    Counter c = Counter(seed())
    int y = &c.fd
    print(y)
